    Salary,
    CASE
        WHEN Salary > 50000 THEN 'High'
        ELSE 'Low'
    END AS SalaryBand
FROM Employees
WHERE SalaryBand = 'High';
```

A. All employees with Salary greater than 50000.
B. All employees with Salary less than or equal to 50000.
C. Query fails with an error because the SELECT alias is not available in WHERE.
D. Empty result set.

## 14. What does MaxSalary represent in the following query?

```sql
SELECT
    Employee,
    Department,
    Salary,
    MAX(Salary) OVER (
        PARTITION BY Department
    ) AS MaxSalary
FROM Employees
WHERE Salary < 50000;
```

A. Maximum salary of the entire Employees table.
B. Maximum salary of each department considering only rows where Salary is less than 50000.
C. Maximum salary of each department considering all employees, regardless of the WHERE condition.
D. Minimum salary of each department.

